Subject: [PATCH 4/5] test(steps): unit-test the suppression rule

The decision - which windows a cleared screen lets through - now lives in
Pickle.Core, away from Verse, so it can be tested without a running game.
Writing the first test found the rule dropping a window whose assembly could
not be read, which is the expensive direction of that mistake: a window of
unknown origin is far likelier to be something the player needs than something
worth dropping. It is let through.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
